                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's early in the game, and I'm already seeing some really sloppy game design. It's very derivative of Portal, which isn't a huge issue on its own, but one of Portal's strengths is that you can't soft lock yourself. Make one mistake in this game, and you have to start the level over. Having to re-solve things you've already solved is annoying and a waste of time.\n\nNot to mention the voice lines, which were clearly written to copy GLaDOS and Cave Johnson, but they are painfully inferior.\n\nThe puzzles themselves can be interesting at times, but I can't recommend a game that forces you to start the level over entirely every time you screw up.",
